Unfortunately due to Covid we have decided to delay our [drum and dance courses](/classes/) until July 20th. Fingers crossed restrictions are lifted and masks can come off! If this doesn't happen we will still go ahead anyway despite the conditions.

Over the next ten weeks in our drum and dance courses, there will be a few extra exciting things happening for students of drum and dance. We will be having a couple of extra rehearsals for Tuesday night dance students and experienced drummers for a show we have coming up at [Strawbfest](https://strawbfest.com.au/) on Friday 11th September. Last year this event was cancelled due to covid, so we are super excited to get back there again. Once again after the performance we will celebrate with strawberry cocktails :) So drummers and dancers lock that date in. Experienced dancers expect a couple of workshops coming up for this event too.

Once again we will be preparing for our end of term drum and dance course gathering. Last term was an absolute blast with once again, amazing food from Sarah at [Homegrown](https://www.facebook.com/homegrownpalmwoods/) Cafe in Palmwoods. So lock in the 19th of September for another evening of DRUM DINNER DANCE. More details to be announced soon [here](https://fb.me/e/55VhNd9Eu).

Check out our photos and videos on our [facebook page](https://www.facebook.com/drumsingdance) from the last gathering!!
